      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T19:48:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The rough assumption is that the vk objects and polling functions are added to their respective queues in the order they are used so encountering an unsignaled/pending fence likely means that all objects after that are also still pending. This might not necessarily always be the case but it seemed like a simple heuristic which could be used to try to minimize the amount of work performed since `PollAndProcessGarbage()` is being used within other functions. WDYT?\n\n\nUpdated to `std::find_if` which IIUC is the function that lets you supply a predicate.",
